    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). AcceptanceTest is the only test class in the project, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the daily owner-creation limit on `POST /api/owners`, rejecting the request with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100 or more owners already carry today's `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`rest/advice/DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` following the existing exception pattern (e.g. `OwnerCityFullException`).\n\n2. **`rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` mapping `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` to `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`, reusing the shared `errorResponse` `ProblemDetail` builder.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 100` constant and a `requireDailyLimitNotReached()` guard invoked from the existing `normalizeAndValidate(...)` pipeline (alongside the analogous per-city check). It counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and throws when the count reaches the cap.\n\nThis mirrors the repo's conventions (a dedicated business-rule exception + centralized advice handler + a guard method in the create pipeline), and only the V1 controller has a create endpoint, so no change was needed in V2.",
